As evening approached, a wealthy man from the town of Qeroah came. His name was Joseph. He had become a follower of Jesus.
He went to Pilate and asked for the body of Jesus. Pilate commanded that he should be given it.
Joseph placed the body in a linen shroud, clean and pure.
He placed it in his new tomb, which he had carved out of the rock. Then he blocked the entrance with a large stone. After that, he left the place.
Mary Magdalene and the other Mary were sitting there opposite the tomb. The guards at the tomb.
Tomorrow was the day after the preparation day. The chief priests and the Pharisees went to Pilate.
They said: "Sir, we remember something that liar said while he was still alive. He claimed that: *After three days I will rise from the dead.*."
So Pilate gave orders for the tomb to be made secure until the third day, otherwise his disciples might come and steal the body and then tell the people that Jesus had risen from the dead, and this last lie would be even worse than the first."
Take some of the guards with you, said Pilatus. Go and do the preservations that are due to the tomb as best as is in your power.
